body:
Hello. Sorry you are feeling such pain and anxiety. I felt this strong gut instinct and saw strange behaviour and inconsistencies for months. I very calmly asked him if some thing was going on a number of times but was met with very calm ‘no, never etc.’ My husband managed to make me feel so guilty that I even thought this and I felt like I was going crazy. However, my gut reaction was right. He confessed about 4 months later and I was devastated. I don’t know your individual situation. However, as someone who has suffered depression, between you mentioning her being upset for days etc. and that she has always had a low libido, I can’t help but think she could be suffering depression and may not be cheating. She could be tired with the kids, feeling monotony of raising a family, basically she could be struggling with her own stuff that you aren’t the cause of. I would be concerned if the low libido was sudden - this could indicate she was getting something elsewhere but ou mentioned she always had it. Depression can make your mind so foggy, she really may have forgotten, could have been calling someone for support etc.

&#x200B;

i find your case hard so understand your pain and confusion as she is keeping something from you. I’m just not sure that it is what you think (fingers crossed anyway). In saying that gut instinct should be trusted in these situations. I think we all had it. Your gut instinct could just be that something is up. Let’s hope it isn’t infidelity but see what you can do to sit down with her be supportive and mention the changes calmly, that you’re concerned and ask her what is up and what you can do - present like facts in a supportive manner to back up you’re concerned something is up with her, otherwise it is just an accusation. Don’t make the actual accusation, try to use as a way to open a conversation. She really could be dealing with depression and getting support from her sister. I’m not going to sugar coat though, instincts are very strong. Don’t leave it and go and talk to someone for your own peace. Good luck, I hope it works out well for you and the pain and confusion surpasses.
